    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1207">

                <pb facs="1338" n="1326" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg1326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79600/7–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05T19:00:00-04:00">July 5, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1113. Info in Depcirtel July 5<anchor n="72" xml:id="d1207-f1"/> may be conveyed
                    to FonOff. At same time you should request Ital Govt to grant US Govt temporary
                    rights for US civil air services (without specific mention TWA<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d1207-f2"/>) to transit and make nontraffic stops in Ital territory
                    as well as right to pick up and set down international traffic in passengers,
                    cargo and mail at Rome. You may also inform Ital Govt that we believe matter of
                    permanent or more definite rights for US airlines and the question <pb
                        facs="1339" n="1327" xml:id="pg1327"/> of reciprocal rights for Ital Govt
                    cannot be discussed until negotiation of peace treaty.</p>
                <p>Substance of foregoing should also be conveyed to your Brit, French and USSR
                    colleagues for info their Govts, adding that we assume their Govts may wish to
                    make similar interim arrangements with Italy covering operation their respective
                    civil air services, in which event we of course have no objection.</p>
                <p>For your info Dept most anxious obtain above rights from Italy soonest possible,
                    particularly in view of activities other countries in reestablishing their own
                    intl air routes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1207-f1" n="72" xml:id="d1207-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed: it reported that the Civil Aeronautics Board, with President
                    Truman’s approval, had announced on July 5, 1945, the issuance of certificates
                    to three United States airlines to operate commercial services over three
                    specified routes. One of the routes included Rome as one of its stops and a
                    second route provided for a connecting link from Madrid to Rome.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1207-f2" n="73" xml:id="d1207-f2-content">
                <p>Transcontinental &amp; Western Air, Inc., the airline authorized by CAB to
                    operate commercial service to Rome.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
